lucene-rust
Copyright 2026 The lucene-rust contributors

This product is a Rust port of Apache Lucene 10.5.0 -- a derivative work of it,
under the Apache License, Version 2.0 -- together with an OpenSearch plugin,
parts of whose engine code are derived from OpenSearch 3.8.0 (each such file
says so in its header). The notices of both follow.

It also contains Rust ports of parts of two Java libraries Lucene's
spatial-extras module depends on, both under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(crates/lucene-util/src/spatial4j and crates/lucene-util/src/s2):

 - Spatial4j 0.8 (https://github.com/locationtech/spatial4j),
   Copyright (c) the Spatial4j contributors (David Smiley et al.),
   a LocationTech project; GeohashUtils came to it from Apache Lucene.
 - The S2 Geometry Library for Java, as published in
   io.sgr:s2-geometry-library-java 1.0.0, Copyright 2005 Google Inc.

crates/lucene-analysis-phonetic reimplements the phonetic encoders of Apache
Commons Codec 1.17.2 (https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-codec/, under
the Apache License, Version 2.0; Copyright 2002-2024 The Apache Software
Foundation) and carries its rule files (src/resources/dmrules.txt and
src/resources/bm/) verbatim. Its NOTICE reads: "Apache Commons Codec /
Copyright 2002-2024 The Apache Software Foundation / This product includes
software developed at The Apache Software Foundation
(https://www.apache.org/)."

crates/lucene-analysis-stempel ports the stemmer-table reader of the Egothor
project's org.egothor.stemmer (src/egothor.rs, src/diff.rs) under the Egothor
Software License version 1.00 (BSD-style; Copyright (C) 1997-2004 Leo
Galambos, (C) 2002-2004 "Egothor developers"), whose text src/egothor.rs
reproduces. This product includes software developed by the Egothor Project.
http://egothor.sf.net/ It also carries Apache Lucene's Polish stemmer table
(stemmer_20000.tbl) and Carrot2's Polish stop word list (BSD).

crates/lucene-analysis-morfologik ports the dictionary lookup of Morfologik
2.1.9 (morfologik-fsa, morfologik-stemming; BSD; Copyright (c) 2006 Dawid
Weiss, (c) 2007-2016 Dawid Weiss, Marcin Milkowski) and carries two
dictionaries: Morfologik's Polish dictionary (morfologik-polish 2.1.9;
Copyright (c) 2016, Marcin Milkowski; BSD 2-Clause, reproduced in
src/resources/polish.LICENSE.txt; data from the SGJP/PoliMorf dictionary of
Polish) and the Ukrainian dictionary of morfologik-ukrainian-search 4.9.1
(Apache License 2.0; based on the dict_uk project,
https://github.com/brown-uk/dict_uk).

crates/lucene-analysis-kuromoji carries the Japanese dictionary Apache
Lucene's analysis-kuromoji jar carries, compiled by Lucene from
mecab-ipadic-2.7.0-20070801 (Nara Institute of Science and Technology; the
mecab-ipadic notice, with ICOT's conditions, is reproduced in the Apache
Lucene NOTICE below), zlib-compressed under src/resources/.

crates/lucene-analysis/src/java_character_tables.rs is generated from the
Unicode Character Database 16.0.0, Copyright (c) 1991-2024 Unicode, Inc.,
under the Unicode License v3, reproduced at the end of this file.

crates/lucene-analysis/src/snowball/algorithms/ is generated by the Snowball
compiler (https://snowballstem.org/, BSD 3-Clause; Copyright (c) 2001 Dr Martin
Porter, (c) 2004-2005 Richard Boulton, (c) 2013 Yoshiki Shibukawa, (c) 2006-2019
Olly Betts) from the Snowball sources Apache Lucene's stemmers come from; the
licence is reproduced in LICENSE.

The test corpus fixtures/corpus/real_polygons.z contains polygons from
Apache Lucene's own tests (Apache License 2.0) and Natural Earth vector
data (public domain, https://www.naturalearthdata.com/).

